        "description": "Slate River Floodplain, Crested Butte, Colorado. The Slate River is a snow-dominated, headwater catchment within the Upper Colorado River Basin and a key testbed for the Floodplain Hydro-Biogeochemistry Science Focus Area at SLAC National Accelerator Laboratory. This portion of the floodplain (~2,700 m elevation) sits downstream of the confluence of Oh Be Joyful (OBJ) Creek and upstream of Gunsight Bridge, on a portion of the river with heavy beaver activity.",
