    "measurementTechnique": [
      "Water level elevation was obtained by subtracting absolute atmospheric pressure from the pressure measured by each transducer. These pressure values were then converted to water level elevation using the depth of the transducer from the top of each piezometer casing and the surveyed elevation of the top of each piezometer casing. Temperature measurements are raw temperature data measured by the sensor. Sensor-derived water levels were compared to water levels manually measured 2-4 times per year and differences are generally <5 cm.",
      "Where possible, absolute atmospheric pressure was determined using either a Campbell Scientific CS100 barometer or an Onset HOBO U20L-04 deployed above ground. However, during periods where either of these data sensors were offline, absolute atmospheric pressure was determined from weather stations several kilometers from the site. The source of atmospheric pressure data used to correct transducer data is listed in the \"DataFlag_02\" column within \"*data.csv\" files.",
      "Most piezometers were surveyed using a real-time kinematic (RTK) global positioning system (GPS). However, for a subset of piezometers, the top of casing elevation was measured using a Trimble total station. Absolute position of the total station was determined by sighting piezometers previously surveyed via RTK."
    ],
